// D17 guard table: one row per test case in .pairingbuddy/scenarios.json.
//
// Row fields:
//   id          test case id (unique)
//   command     the Bash command or tool call; an array means several calls, each its own test
//   runState    "none" | "run" | "unit" (run = run/task/ledger.json, no unit.json; unit = run/unit.json, with or without a ledger)
//   context     "subagent" | "main"
//   expect      "allow" | "deny"
//   also        optional extra cells { runState, context } the same case covers
//   setup       optional condition the row needs beyond runState/context
//   message     optional RegExp the deny reason must match, besides the rule
//   forbid      optional RegExp the deny reason must not match
//
// Rows run in two places. tests/js/d17-rules.test.mjs runs a row straight against d17Denial in a repo of plain files, and
// tests/js/d17-guard.test.mjs runs the rows that need the real hook process (a `setup` that builds a run, a session, a broken
// plugin copy or a payload shape, or a `<plugin>` path) through hooks/gate-boot.mjs. Every `also` cell and every command of an
// array `command` is its own test, named after the row id.
//
// More fields:
//   rule        the rule family a deny must come from (names in tests/js/d17-cases.mjs): a name, a list of names, or an
//               object by run state ({ none, run, unit, otherwise }). A scenario's `rule` is the default for its rows.
//   pin         true when the row records what the guard does today (a known gap or a choice), not what it must do

